  "source": {
    "source_id": "companion:sphmc-standardized-rgo-relative-entropy",
    "anchor": "S3.E2/S4.Ex3 actual proximal point; S4.Ex8 standardized posterior; S4.SS1.p4.2-p4.3/FIRST S4.E6 omitted canonical entropy domains.",
    "original_text": "Exact primary actual proximal/posterior/standardization and omitted entropy context. Uniqueness and canonical entropy below are authored background; FIRST4.6 inequality remains OPEN.\n\nANCHOR S2.p1.1\n<p id=\"S2.p1.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">Except in the generic warm start result <a href=\"#S6.Thmtheorem1\" title=\"Theorem 6.1 (Recursive warm start generator). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">Theorem</span> <span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">6.1</span></a>\nand its consequence <a href=\"#S7.Thmtheorem1\" title=\"Theorem 7.1 (Picard HMC warm starts). ‣ 7.1 Picard HMC warm starts ‣ 7 Picard HMC warm starts and the high-accuracy sampler ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">Theorem</span> <span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">7.1</span></a>, throughout the remainder of the paper\n<math id=\"S2.p1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"V\\in C^{2}(\\mathbb{R}^{d})\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V\\in C^{2}(\\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and (<a href=\"#S1.E1\" title=\"Equation 1.1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">1.1</span></a>) holds pointwise.\nFor most of the paper, we normalize <math id=\"S2.p1.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\beta=1\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id=\"S2.p1.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\kappa^{-1}I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}V\\preceq I\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace=\"0.167em\">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\kappa^{-1}I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}V\\preceq I</annotation></semantics></math>; this can be achieved by rescaling.</p>\nANCHOR S3.SS1.p1.1\n<p id=\"S3.SS1.p1.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">For a smoothing variance\n<math id=\"S3.SS1.p1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\eta&gt;0\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, write</p>\nANCHOR S3.E2\n<table id=\"S3.E2\" class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table\">\n\n<tbody><tr class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline\">\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft\"></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center\"><math id=\"S3.E2.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\widehat{g}_{\\eta}(y;G)\\coloneqq\\nabla V\\bigl(\\operatorname{prox}_{\\eta V}(y)+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,G\\bigr)\\,,\\qquad G\\sim\\mathsf{N}(0,I)\\,.\" display=\"block\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace=\"0.167em\">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize=\"1.200em\" minsize=\"1.200em\">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace=\"0.170em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize=\"1.200em\" minsize=\"1.200em\" rspace=\"0.170em\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace=\"2.167em\">,</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace=\"0.170em\">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\widehat{g}_{\\eta}(y;G)\\coloneqq\\nabla V\\bigl(\\operatorname{prox}_{\\eta V}(y)+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,G\\bigr)\\,,\\qquad G\\sim\\mathsf{N}(0,I)\\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright\"></td>\n<td rowspan=\"1\" class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right\">(3.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>\n</table>\nANCHOR S4.Ex3\n<table id=\"S4.Ex3\" class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table\">\n\n<tbody><tr class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline\">\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft\"></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center\"><math id=\"S4.Ex3.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"x_{y}^{+}\\coloneqq\\operatorname{prox}_{\\eta V}(y)\\,.\" display=\"block\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace=\"0.170em\">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_{y}^{+}\\coloneqq\\operatorname{prox}_{\\eta V}(y)\\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright\"></td></tr></tbody>\n</table>\nANCHOR S4.Ex8\n<table id=\"S4.Ex8\" class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table\">\n\n<tbody><tr class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline\">\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft\"></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center\"><math id=\"S4.Ex8.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\rho_{y}(u)\\coloneqq V(x_{y}^{+}+\\sqrt{\\eta}u)-V(x_{y}^{+})-\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,\\langle\\nabla V(x_{y}^{+}),u\\rangle\\,.\" display=\"block\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace=\"0.170em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace=\"0.167em\">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace=\"0.170em\">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho_{y}(u)\\coloneqq V(x_{y}^{+}+\\sqrt{\\eta}u)-V(x_{y}^{+})-\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,\\langle\\nabla V(x_{y}^{+}),u\\rangle\\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright\"></td></tr></tbody>\n</table>\nANCHOR S4.SS1.p4.2\n<p id=\"S4.SS1.p4.2\" class=\"ltx_p\"><span id=\"S4.SS1.p4.2.1\" class=\"ltx_text\">Then <math id=\"S4.SS1.p4.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"0\\preceq\\nabla^{2}\\rho_{y}\\preceq\\eta I\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace=\"0.167em\">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\preceq\\nabla^{2}\\rho_{y}\\preceq\\eta I</annotation></semantics></math>, and under <math id=\"S4.SS1.p4.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"R_{\\eta,y}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_{\\eta,y}</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math id=\"S4.SS1.p4.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"(X-x_{y}^{+})/\\sqrt{\\eta}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(X-x_{y}^{+})/\\sqrt{\\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> has density\nproportional to <math id=\"S4.SS1.p4.m5\" class=\"ltx_math_unparsed\" alttext=\"u\\mapsto e^{-\\lVert u\\rVert^{2}/2-\\rho_{y}(u)}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">↦</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo fence=\"true\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">∥</mo><mi>u</mi><mo fence=\"true\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u\\mapsto e^{-\\lVert u\\rVert^{2}/2-\\rho_{y}(u)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Call this law <math id=\"S4.SS1.p4.m6\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\mathsf{r}_{y}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathsf{r}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nWe have</span></p>\nANCHOR S4.SS1.p4.3\n<p id=\"S4.SS1.p4.3\" class=\"ltx_p\"><span id=\"S4.SS1.p4.3.1\" class=\"ltx_text\">Indeed, the first inequality combines Talagrand’s inequality for the standard\nGaussian with the Gaussian log-Sobolev inequality; the second uses that\n<math id=\"S4.SS1.p4.m7\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\nabla\\rho_{y}(0)=0\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace=\"0.167em\">∇</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\nabla\\rho_{y}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id=\"S4.SS1.p4.m8\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\nabla\\rho_{y}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace=\"0.167em\">∇</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\nabla\\rho_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id=\"S4.SS1.p4.m9\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\eta\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\eta</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz; and the last\nfollows by integration by parts since <math id=\"S4.SS1.p4.m10\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\mathsf{r}_{y}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathsf{r}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id=\"S4.SS1.p4.m11\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"1\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1</annotation></semantics></math>-strongly\nlog-concave with its mode at <math id=\"S4.SS1.p4.m12\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"0\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>\nANCHOR S4.E6\n<table id=\"S4.E6\" class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table\">\n\n<tbody><tr class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline\">\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft\"></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center\"><math id=\"S4.E6.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"W_{2}(\\mathsf{r}_{y},\\mathsf{N}(0,I))\\leqslant\\sqrt{\\mathbb{E}_{\\mathsf{r}_{y}}[\\lVert\\nabla\\rho_{y}(U)\\rVert^{2}]}\\leqslant\\eta\\sqrt{\\mathbb{E}_{\\mathsf{r}_{y}}\\lVert U\\rVert^{2}}\\leqslant\\eta\\sqrt{d}\\,.\" display=\"block\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace=\"0.167em\">∇</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence=\"true\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" rspace=\"0em\">∥</mo><mi>U</mi><mo fence=\"true\" lspace=\"0em\">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace=\"0.170em\">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W_{2}(\\mathsf{r}_{y},\\mathsf{N}(0,I))\\leqslant\\sqrt{\\mathbb{E}_{\\mathsf{r}_{y}}[\\lVert\\nabla\\rho_{y}(U)\\rVert^{2}]}\\leqslant\\eta\\sqrt{\\mathbb{E}_{\\mathsf{r}_{y}}\\lVert U\\rVert^{2}}\\leqslant\\eta\\sqrt{d}\\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright\"></td>\n<td rowspan=\"1\" class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right\">(4.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>\n</table>",
    "text_sha256": "3ead07cc8aeec2ab9905c68ee3d7ae2f2ab104c0aac3b50f45aeb97812075f19"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.StandardizedRGORelativeEntropy.standardized_rgo_unique_prox_and_finite_entropy",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/SmoothedPicardHMC/StandardizedRGORelativeEntropy.lean",
    "statement": "{E S : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [CompleteSpace E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    [MeasurableSpace S] {V : E → ℝ} {κ : ℝ}\n    (hκ : 1 ≤ κ) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)\n    (hH : ∀ x v : E, κ⁻¹*‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v v ∧\n      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v v ≤ ‖v‖^2)\n    {eta : S → ℝ} {y : S → E} (heta : Measurable eta) (hy : Measurable y)\n    (hpos : ∀ s, 0 < eta s) :\n    ∃ p : S → E, Measurable p ∧\n      (∀ s, p s+eta s • gradient V (p s)=y s) ∧\n      (∀ s z, z+eta s • gradient V z=y s → z=p s) ∧\n      let rho := fun s u => V (p s+Real.sqrt (eta s) • u)-V (p s)-\n        Real.sqrt (eta s)*inner ℝ (gradient V (p s)) u\n      let mu := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n      let R := fun s => mu.tilted (fun x => -‖x-y s‖^2/(2*eta s))\n      let r := fun s => (R s).map (fun x => (Real.sqrt (eta s))⁻¹ • (x-p s))\n      let gamma := stdGaussian E\n      let Z := fun s => ∫ u, Real.exp (-rho s u) ∂gamma\n      let q := fun s u => Real.exp (-rho s u)/Z s\n      ∀ s, r s ≪ gamma ∧\n        _root_.InformationTheory.klDiv (r s) gamma ≠ ⊤ ∧\n        Integrable (MeasureTheory.llr (r s) gamma) (r s) ∧\n        MeasureTheory.llr (r s) gamma =ᵐ[r s] (fun u => Real.log (q s u)) ∧\n        Integrable (rho s) (r s) ∧\n        (_root_.InformationTheory.klDiv (r s) gamma).toReal =\n          (∫ u, q s u*Real.log (q s u) ∂gamma) ∧\n        (_root_.InformationTheory.klDiv (r s) gamma).toReal =\n          -(∫ u, rho s u ∂r s)-Real.log (Z s)",
    "statement_sha256": "7a3fabb04f0008c3b3075843c4815dfe2c2f982c73ed32f893cbdbdf0e383a32",
    "compiled": true
  },
  "blind_reconstruction": {
    "text": "Let E be a complete finite-dimensional real Hilbert space, equipped with its Borel structure and canonical volume, and let S be an arbitrary measurable space. Dimension zero is permitted. Let V:E→ℝ be C² and κ≥1, with\n  (1/κ)‖v‖² ≤ D²V(x)[v,v] ≤ ‖v‖²\nfor all x,v∈E. Let η:S→ℝ and y:S→E be measurable, with η(s)>0 for every s.\nThere exists a measurable p:S→E such that, for every s,\n  p(s)+η(s)∇V(p(s))=y(s),\nand every z∈E satisfying z+η(s)∇V(z)=y(s) equals p(s).\nUsing this same p throughout, define\n  ρ_s(u)=V(p(s)+√η(s) u)−V(p(s))−√η(s)⟨∇V(p(s)),u⟩,\n  μ=volume.tilted(x↦−V(x)),\n  R_s=μ.tilted(x↦−‖x−y(s)‖²/(2η(s))),\n  r_s=(x↦(√η(s))⁻¹(x−p(s)))_* R_s,\n  γ=the centered covariance-identity Gaussian on E,\n  Z_s=∫exp(−ρ_s(u))dγ(u),\n  q_s(u)=exp(−ρ_s(u))/Z_s.\nHere each tilt is the normalized exponential tilt when its exponential weight is integrable, and the zero measure otherwise. For every s, r_s is absolutely continuous with respect to γ, and its canonical extended-nonnegative-real KL divergence from γ is finite. Its canonical log-likelihood representative llr(r_s,γ) and ρ_s are integrable with respect to r_s. The identity llr(r_s,γ)(u)=log(q_s(u)) holds r_s-almost everywhere. Furthermore,\n  KL(r_s‖γ).toReal = ∫q_s(u)log(q_s(u))dγ(u)\n                   = −∫ρ_s(u)dr_s(u)−log(Z_s).\nThe statement supplies p internally, places no upper bound on positive η, and requires no separately supplied stationary selector, probability, normalization, integrability or entropy certificate. The almost-everywhere identity does not assert pointwise equality of the chosen log-likelihood representative.",
    "text_sha256": "a149e16cf033067c2bcca1e8bd6b3885e595e7806e2be544f75f71ab0994e9bb",
    "decoder": "blind_statement_decoder_33",
    "decoder_packet_sha256": "9c4839d6d07eee8a1a4d83ddcbca49032191453213684038d36897ef225480e2",
    "decoder_run_sha256": "60a931cb2dcd3a85a649a823a627804b97570d72b1221ad12faf271c88b10287",
    "source_text_visible": false
  },
