        "Authored measurable family S with measurable eta/y, every eta(s)>0. Constant Unit specializes printed fixed parameters. Stationary uniqueness is an internally proved conclusion."
      ],
      "statement": "Under unchanged normalized source curvature and C2 assumptions, produce the measurable uniquely stationary proximal point and the true affine standardized posterior; prove canonical KL finite, canonical llr L1 and only AE equality with the literal logdensity, actual residual L1 and both exact real entropy identities for every eta>0.",
      "formula": "p_s+\\eta_s\\nabla V(p_s)=y_s,\\quad\\mathrm{KL}(r_s\\Vert\\gamma)<\\infty,\\quad\\log\\frac{dr_s}{d\\gamma}=\\log q_s\\quad r_s\\text{-a.e.},\\quad\\mathrm{KL}(r_s\\Vert\\gamma)=\\int q_s\\log q_s\\,d\\gamma=-\\mathbb E_{r_s}\\rho_s-\\log Z_s.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Keep one actual posterior and its proved density domains",
          "text": "Reuse the true posterior square-root producer once. It constructs the same measurable p, residual rho, true RGO R and affine standardized r used throughout this theorem. Its positive actual Z, actual probability and qlogq L1 are conclusions, not source inputs.",
          "formula": "R_s=\\mu^{[-\\|x-y_s\\|^2/(2\\eta_s)]},\\quad r_s=(x\\mapsto\\eta_s^{-1/2}(x-p_s))_\\#R_s=\\gamma^{[-\\rho_s]},\\quad q_s=e^{-\\rho_s}/Z_s,\\quad0<Z_s\\le1.",
          "lean": "StandardizedRGOSqrtDensity.standardized_rgo_sqrt_density_domain"
        },
        {
          "title": "Derive stationary uniqueness from the actual source curvature",
          "text": "The Hessian lower bound produces strong convexity and hence nonnegative gradient monotonicity. Subtract two stationary equations and take inner product with z-p. Positive eta forces norm(z-p)=0. This derived uniqueness permits future identification of independently constructed stationary witnesses; no witness equality is assumed here.",
          "formula": "\\langle\\nabla V(z)-\\nabla V(p),z-p\\rangle\\ge\\kappa^{-1}\\|z-p\\|^2\\ge0,\\quad0=\\|z-p\\|^2+\\eta\\langle\\nabla V(z)-\\nabla V(p),z-p\\rangle\\Longrightarrow z=p.",
          "lean": "HessianStrongConvexity.strongConvexOn_univ_of_fderiv2_lower; StrongConvexFirstOrder.gradient_inner_lower_bound_of_strongConvexOn; actual hzero/hi"
        },
        {
          "title": "Transfer the genuine entropy domain to the actual tilted law",
          "text": "Positivity of the already proved actual integral Z rules out a nonintegrable exponential. qlogq L1 gives exp(-rho)logq L1 by multiplying with Z, and the actual tilted integrability equivalence gives logq L1r. Since logq=-rho-logZ everywhere and r is probability, rho is L1r as well.",
          "formula": "\\log q_s=-\\rho_s-\\log Z_s,\\quad e^{-\\rho_s}\\log q_s=Z_s q_s\\log q_s,\\quad\\log q_s\\in L^1(r_s),\\quad\\rho_s\\in L^1(r_s).",
          "lean": "integral_undef contradiction with actual positiveZ; Real.log_div; integrable_tilted_iff; actual he.const_mul/hlogi/hρi"
        },
        {
          "title": "Use the existing canonical KL producer and AE log-ratio adapter",
          "text": "Apply the shared TiltedKL theorem to the actual Gaussian base with exponents -rho and0; the zero tilt is gamma. The separately compiled log-ratio adapter identifies canonical llr with logq only r-a.e. This transfers L1 and integrals, and proves extended KL is not infinity. It supplies no pointwise RN derivative.",
          "formula": "\\operatorname{llr}(r_s,\\gamma)=\\log q_s\\quad r_s\\text{-a.e.},\\quad\\operatorname{llr}(r_s,\\gamma)\\in L^1(r_s),\\quad\\mathrm{KL}(r_s\\Vert\\gamma)<\\infty.",
          "lean": "TiltedKL.finite_klDiv_and_toReal_eq_integral_normalizedLogRatio; TiltedLogRatio.llr_tilted_tilted_ae; actual hrep/hzeroTilt"
        },
        {
          "title": "Integrate both exact entropy formulas under the same laws",
          "text": "The actual tilted integral rewrites integral_r logq to integral_gamma qlogq. Its everywhere explicit logarithm and the proved rho/constant L1 domains give -integral_r rho-logZ. The canonical finite KL real value equals both. No original V partition, Gaussian-volume constant or affine Jacobian is added to this relative Gaussian formula.",
          "formula": "\\mathrm{KL}(r_s\\Vert\\gamma)=\\int\\log q_s\\,dr_s=\\int q_s\\log q_s\\,d\\gamma=-\\int\\rho_s\\,dr_s-\\log Z_s.",
          "lean": "integral_tilted; integral_sub; integral_neg; integral_const; actual hkl/hwint/hentropy"
        }
      ],
      "lean_statement": "Under unchanged normalized source curvature and C2 assumptions, produce the measurable uniquely stationary proximal point and the true affine standardized posterior; prove canonical KL finite, canonical llr L1 and only AE equality with the literal logdensity, actual residual L1 and both exact real entropy identities for every eta>0.",
      "lean_proof": "Keep one actual posterior and its proved density domains; Derive stationary uniqueness from the actual source curvature; Transfer the genuine entropy domain to the actual tilted law; Use the existing canonical KL producer and AE log-ratio adapter; Integrate both exact entropy formulas under the same laws",
